[bharat@delta.uucp (R. Bharat Rao) writes:]
[] Basically what good are fountains anyway?

both good and bad things can happen when you dip or quaff from a
fountain. you can gain an intrinsic attribute or summon a monster.
you cannot get a blessed item from a fountain with one exception.
it is possible that curses and magic might fade. play with it, you
may die a lot (but hopefully not the same way twice).

btw, you really need to experiment with other characters, especially
a priest, at least once.

[] 2. How in the world do you use a spellbook? I tried reading it, and
[] was told I memorized the runes. Thanks a lot, but how does tha help
[] me?

this is explained in the guidebook which is also recommended!
basically now that you've memorized the spell you can cast it,
("Z"ap) assuming you can handle the effort, which requires
certain wizardly attributes.

[] 3. Must sacrifices only be done with fresh meat? I ran across a

for anything interesting to happen, the corpse must be fresh (if you
can't eat it safely why should the gods be happy with it? some corpses
are inherently less fresh than others). the other half of the equation
is using the "right" altar, ":" look at it. strange things happen when
you appeal to gods not of your alignment or when you don't quite
keep your god happy. unfortunately you'll have to use uncommon sense
in this regard since there are no clues...

[] 4. In general when you find lots of armor should you don whatever you
[] can? Like +0 elven cloak, a black cap (+0 something else etc.), or

chances are that more than not you'll be okay but the problem is that
when you get that cursed item it could significantly alter your game!!!
it is best to divine the blessed state of your armor before trying it
on. armor gets better with improved enchantments (i.e. a blessed +6
black cap) and some armors are inherently better than others because
they provide more protection and have intrinsic attributes as well,
(gauntlets of power are an obvious example).

[] 5. Should you just sell all extra stuff to shopkeepers?

well, by this course you'll get more gold and so when you die because
you don't have needed magic you'll have a higher score than otherwise.
on the other hand, if you could manipulate magic then those seemingly
worthless items might in fact be more valuable than gold. consider
these rumors:
They say that a blank scroll is like a blank check.
They say that a wand of cancellation is like a wand of polymorph.
They say that a wand of cancellation is nothing like a wand of polymorph.
They say that the magic marker is mightier than the sword.

